d #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{35}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292985} {:answer/id #uuid "14d56cac-ed17-5710-841c-febbaf99df41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{30}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293018} {:answer/id #uuid "1c85e6c0-f9c5-59fd-82f4-b7d8d7bfef47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{45}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293050} {:answer/id #uuid "b1627ee8-4d51-52a6-8929-c4107d5d9df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{40}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293626} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d4b089-0b2e-50ee-85b5-fddac40bfb50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{37}^{∘}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293649}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292985} :answer-field/id #uuid "4393158b-4653-59fb-b173-c91805421904" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a35f6859-2f6e-53eb-b636-6ed7f822bc20" :question/math-academy-id "q-27826" :question/problem "![](images/81/812e1c08b671e54023a65dc5b9fbf089ddd27781ad555d6fb9e4d2a9816d193f.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $△ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{AH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ If $m∠ACB={125}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠HAC.$" :question/worked-solution "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠ACB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{125}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={55}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△AHC$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {55}^{∘}+m∠HAC+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{145}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={35}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "10a1f6ef-362d-5631-86f1-b71f57ec2d11" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567149}} {:db/id #edb/ref 175921